          "message": "feat(menu): the Game frame rate cap, Descriptor reuse and Sampler cache apply in play (#7)\n\nThe three rows took a restart only because their values were read once at the start.\n\n- Game frame rate cap: host/nn_vi.c reads the row at each present (HOS_OPT_FPS_CAP, 53, through the\n  renderer's existing option callback; no MkwVkHost/MkwVkRenderer change), the vsync thread re-reads\n  its period each tick, and a cap brought down gives the game back its own limiter (+0xfc), its rate\n  (+0x2c8) and its step (hos_frame_seconds_bits). The FPS counter's line follows the row. HOS_FPS_MAX\n  still holds the cap for a run.\n- Descriptor reuse and Sampler cache: the menu tells vk_draw.cpp the rows at load and on each change\n  (menu_debug_rows). A draw keeps descriptors only from a build made with the same setting, so turning\n  reuse on never trusts a build that recorded no slot versions. RX_VK_DESC_REUSE and\n  RX_VK_SAMPLER_CACHE still hold them for a run.\n\nChecks: tests/test_frame_rate_cap_step.py gains the cap changed in play (up, down, Uncapped, back to\n60, and with HOS_FPS_STEP=0); tests/test_menu_env_on.py the Debug rows changed in play.\n\n---\nMoved from NotRexed/Hookshot#2900 (closed when the GitHub account was suspended).\n\nCo-authored-by: hckrman101 <239247847+hckrman101@users.noreply.github.com>\nReviewed-on: https://git.magicbean.dev/MagicBeanDev/Longshot/pulls/7\n",
